{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2184 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "9c76a656a4122227cf9342babe1771461e7024453fee13f6ec57f308810cb36d" :edb/db-before-t 2183 :edb/db-after-t 2184 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535496 50 #inst "2026-10-09T01:14:29.666Z" 13194139535496 true] [17592186119764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186352126 13194139535496 true] [17592186119764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186352140 13194139535496 true] [17592186119765 1020 #edb/ref 17592186352133 13194139535496 true] [17592186119765 1020 #edb/ref 17592186352147 13194139535496 true] [17592186120229 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535496 true] [17592186120229 1100 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(2, 1, 3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $3x - 6y - 6z =-15$." 13194139535496 false] [17592186120229 1100 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(2,1,3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $3x-6y-6z=-15.$" 13194139535496 true] [17592186120229 1145 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=-1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-6y-6z & =-15 \\\\ 3(1)-6(-1)-6z & =-15 \\\\ -6z & =-24 \\\\ z & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,-1,4)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-1,4⟩-⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨3,-6,-6⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 3+(-2)\\cdot (-6)+1\\cdot (-6)|}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-6)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-3+12-6|}{\\sqrt{9+36+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352126 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352127 13194139535496 true] [17592186352126 1089 "q-129103" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352126 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535496 true] [17592186352126 1100 "Given that $Q(3,-4,5)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,-4⟩=-42$, find the shortest distance from $P(1,-5,2)$ to $Π.$" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352126 1113 #uuid "615c5d14-edd0-5400-879a-9ac3f8e46383" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352126 1145 "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨3,-4,5⟩-⟨1,-5,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨-2,4,-4⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4+4-12|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-12|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{6} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352127 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352128 13194139535496 true] [17592186352127 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352129 13194139535496 true] [17592186352127 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352130 13194139535496 true] [17592186352127 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352131 13194139535496 true] [17592186352127 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352132 13194139535496 true] [17592186352127 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535496 true] [17592186352127 1041 "selection" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352127 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352129 13194139535496 true] [17592186352127 1110 #uuid "b94cdc40-8dc6-5650-b26a-c04a34377621" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352128 1034 "3" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352128 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352128 1111 #uuid "e72812f6-6a06-5459-8603-1289e1be6eb1" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352129 1034 "2" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352129 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352129 1111 #uuid "9aeecabb-db14-540a-9f16-270377121196" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352130 1034 "1" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352130 1111 #uuid "97a88135-2962-5bd1-9e53-1e14413c3440" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352131 1034 "4" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352131 1111 #uuid "30e0b430-2e7c-532b-85e0-a7f88c052428" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352132 1034 "5" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352132 1111 #uuid "d7f830de-c7a2-5616-afc7-916cfa6c4100" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352133 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352134 13194139535496 true] [17592186352133 1089 "q-129163" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352133 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535496 true] [17592186352133 1100 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-2,5,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $4x-4y+2z=2.$" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352133 1113 #uuid "8b6ae898-0635-54c5-a55e-aacad2ce72c9" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352133 1145 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-4y+2z & =2 \\\\ 4(1)-4(1)+2z & =2 \\\\ 2z & =2 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,1,1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,1⟩-⟨-2,5,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-4,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨4,-4,2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|3\\cdot 4+(-4)\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12+16+8|}{\\sqrt{16+16+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|36|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{6} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352134 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352135 13194139535496 true] [17592186352134 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352136 13194139535496 true] [17592186352134 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352137 13194139535496 true] [17592186352134 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352138 13194139535496 true] [17592186352134 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352139 13194139535496 true] [17592186352134 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535496 true] [17592186352134 1041 "selection" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352134 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352137 13194139535496 true] [17592186352134 1110 #uuid "7b8abed5-7b3e-5cbc-89ed-00237df2fd1e" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352135 1034 "\\frac{23}{6}" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352135 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352135 1111 #uuid "8db587ce-69aa-581a-be6a-29d92bf6b14e" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352136 1034 "7" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352136 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352136 1111 #uuid "42e846d8-f031-5281-a2b2-dc7db84e8aa0" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352137 1034 "6" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352137 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352137 1111 #uuid "48209447-a767-5708-b0d0-1ff8956e3296" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352138 1034 "\\frac{17}{6}" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352138 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352138 1111 #uuid "d867d796-7544-56a4-84f1-87fc57408402" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352139 1034 "5" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352139 1111 #uuid "aafb01de-a3ee-585a-be34-e44b278c8b13" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352140 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352141 13194139535496 true] [17592186352140 1089 "q-33454" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352140 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535496 true] [17592186352140 1100 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(4,-2,7)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩=27.$" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352140 1113 #uuid "088dd097-0f42-5df8-97da-74581538794b" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352140 1145 "First, we need to find a point on the plane. If $r=⟨x,y,z⟩,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,3⟩ & =27 \\\\ -3x+2y+3z & =27 \\\\ 3z & =27+3x-2y \\\\ z & =9+x-\\frac{2}{3}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting $x=6$ and $y=3,$ we get \n\n$$\nz=9+6-\\frac{2}{3}(3)=13.\n$$\n\nSo, the point $Q(6,3,13)$ lies on the plane. \n\nNow, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨6,3,13⟩-⟨4,-2,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,5,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of a plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-3,2,3⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+10+18|}{\\sqrt{9+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|22|}{\\sqrt{22}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{22}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352142 13194139535496 true] [17592186352141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352143 13194139535496 true] [17592186352141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352144 13194139535496 true] [17592186352141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352145 13194139535496 true] [17592186352141 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352146 13194139535496 true] [17592186352141 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535496 true] [17592186352141 1041 "selection" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352141 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352144 13194139535496 true] [17592186352141 1110 #uuid "bea90a28-9d85-5ebf-9862-ad129369fe84" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352142 1034 "12" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352142 1111 #uuid "51676e50-b7f0-5eed-97fd-1d3a493444f8" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352143 1034 "\\sqrt{11}" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352143 1111 #uuid "7417c09d-0a95-532b-8866-0a6e02280014" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352144 1034 "\\sqrt{22}" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352144 1111 #uuid "28f5b5fa-ac8e-5c0c-a526-a48566199827" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352145 1034 "7" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352145 1111 #uuid "487132b9-07c4-5126-93d7-c72103039bd2" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352146 1034 "5" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352146 1111 #uuid "a03e5b55-0198-5d77-b267-35bc98a33873" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352147 1017 #edb/ref 17592186352148 13194139535496 true] [17592186352147 1089 "q-80117" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352147 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535496 true] [17592186352147 1100 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,4,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $6x-3y+6z=-18.$" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352147 1113 #uuid "41b27e53-413c-5bbb-b780-1b6a9c1ad103" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352147 1145 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-3y+6z & =-18 \\\\ 6(1)-3(2)+6z & =-18 \\\\ 6z & =-18 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,2,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,2,-3⟩-⟨5,4,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨6,-3,6⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-24+6+6|}{\\sqrt{36+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,-12\\,|}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352149 13194139535496 true] [17592186352148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352150 13194139535496 true] [17592186352148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352151 13194139535496 true] [17592186352148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352152 13194139535496 true] [17592186352148 1000 #edb/ref 17592186352153 13194139535496 true] [17592186352148 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535496 true] [17592186352148 1041 "selection" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352148 1104 #edb/ref 17592186352150 13194139535496 true] [17592186352148 1110 #uuid "d9ddf0a5-caf2-58f2-b0f2-8ae4f18c0136" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352149 1034 "3" 13194139535496 true] [17592186352149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535496 true] [17592186352149 1111 #uuid "c62d49e3-b